# bix-43-q1  CBD/cisplatin combination vs DMSO -> GO Biological Process enrichment (gseapy prerank)

## What ran (analysis/analysis.py, ~40 s, deterministic seed 42)
1. Preprocessing: 63,677 x 30 raw counts -> 53,636 ENSG->symbol mapped -> drop 10,041 unmapped ->
   collapse multi-ENSG symbols by summing counts -> filter counts>=10 in >=3 samples -> 18,100 symbols.
   (1,416 of those "symbols" are ENSG IDs used as gene_name by the annotation file and can never match a GMT.)
2. DE: DESeq2-equivalent NB2 GLM re-implemented in numpy (~ 0 + Group, all 30 samples, median-of-ratios
   size factors, df-corrected method-of-moments dispersion shrunk to the mean-dispersion trend,
   Wald contrast Cisplatin_IC50_CBD_IC50 - DMSO, t(residual df=20) reference).
   Self-calibration on matched simulated nulls: type-I error 0.047 at nominal 0.05; 86% power for a 1.8x spike.
3. Sensitivities: additive treatment+serum_starvation design, leave-out-3_1, starved combination vs starved DMSO.
4. Ranked lists: primary log2FoldChange (+ -log10(padj)xsign, + signal-to-noise), universes A (18,100) and B (12,910).
5. gseapy-equivalent prerank engine (nblib.Prerank): validated on synthetic spiked lists, size filters,
   known-answer sets, determinism, and a random-set null control on the real metric.
6. gseapy_one_shot.py: the literal gp.prerank(..., gene_sets="GO_Biological_Process_2021") call, ready to run.

## BLOCKED (not an analytical choice, an environment limit)
The sandbox has no route to any network host (Errno 101 to raw IPs), pip cannot reach any index,
there is no R, and a filesystem scan of every mount finds no gseapy, no *.gmt, no GO/Enrichr/MSigDB/
org.Hs.eg.db/GO.db artefact. So `gseapy` + `GO_Biological_Process_2021` cannot be executed here and the
enrichment result (the answer to the question) is NOT produced by this capsule run.

## To unblock, provide ONE of
* network egress to maayanlab.cloud + `pip install gseapy`, then `python analysis/gseapy_one_shot.py`; or
* the file `data/GO_Biological_Process_2021.gmt` (Enrichr export, gene symbols). With the GMT alone the
  validated engine in nblib.Prerank reproduces the gseapy prerank semantics (15-500 size filter,
  1000 permutations, seed 42, BH FDR across gene sets) and prints the lowest-FDR term, ~2-4 min runtime.

